{
  "name": "happy",
  "integration": "illumio-core",
  "description": "A small estate below the 500-object synchronous cap. Proves the label catalog bootstrap resolves bare label hrefs on a workload, that the per-workload N+1 GET is what supplies open_service_ports (the collection response carries none), that an IANA protocol number is converted and a portless protocol counted rather than invented into a Service, that a 0.0.0.0 bind is rewritten to the workload's own address, that loopback and docker-bridge interfaces never reach an interface, and that a deleted workload, a workload with no href, and a non-object element are each skipped with a count. wl-0004 carries an updated_at a year in the future: the platform rejects an entire record whose timestamp is after now, so the clamp in _parse_ts is what keeps that asset.",
